
How to Generate the ice_HaloUpdate and ice_gather/scatter subroutines quickly

generate_HaloUpdate.sh and generate_GatherScatter.sh are scripts that generate 
the multiple ice_HaloUpdate calls in ice_boundary.F90 and the ice_gather/scatter 
calls in ice_gather_scatter.F90 to keep them all self-consistent.  
The script uses a template to generate the various overloaded subroutines 
depending on dimension, data type, and other factors.  It supports both serial and mpi
code.

generate_HaloUpdate.sh and generate_GatherScatter.sh create files for each 
subroutine with a name that ends in .subr.  Those files are catted into *_all.subr
file and can replace the code in between "autogenerate start" and "autogenerate end"
in ice_boundary.F90 and ice_gather_scatter.F90 respectively.

The recommended usage is described below.

1. Verify the current version of generate_HaloUpdate.sh and generate_GatherScatter.sh
 
  cd cicecore/cicedyn/infrastructure/comm/mpi
   ./generate_HaloUpdate.sh
   ./generate_GatherScatter.sh

  ! Verify generate_HaloUpdate.sh produces code in HaloUpdate_all.subr that matches the current 
  ! implementation in ice_boundary.F90.  If it doesn't, it suggests someone made manual changes to 
  ! the subroutines in ice_boundary.F90.  Try to reconcile those differences and update 
  ! generate_HaloUpdate.sh first, then move forward.
  ! Do the same for generate_GatherScatter, GatherScatter_all.subr, and ice_gather_scatter.F90.

  ! Now copy the current output.

  cp haloUpdate_all.subr haloUpdate_all.subr.current
  cp GatherScatter_all.subr GatherScatter_all.subr.current

2. Update generate_HaloUpdate.sh and/or generate_GatherScatter.sh and generate new subroutines

  ! Modify generate_HaloUpdate.sh and/or generate_GatherScatter.sh to generate updated code then run

  ./generate_HaloUpdate.sh
  diff haloUpdate_all.subr.current haloUpdate_all.subr

  and/or

  ./generate_GatherScatter.sh
  diff GatherScatter_all.subr.current GatherScatter_all.subr

  ! Review diffences with the current code (HaloUpdate_all.current)

3. Update the source code, ice_boundary.F90 and/or ice_gather_scatter.F90

  ! When the changes are reasonable and as expected, edit ice_boundary.F90, cut out the code
  ! between "autogenerate start" and "autogenerate end" and replace that code with the latest 
  ! HaloUpdate_all.subr file.
  ! Do the same with ice_gather_scatter.F90 and GatherScatter_all.subr.

  cp ice_boundary.F90 ice_boundary.F90.current
  ! edit ice_boundary.F90, replace subroutines with HaloUpdate_all.subr
  diff ice_boundary.F90.current ice_boundary.F90

  cp ice_gather_scatter.F90 ice_gather_scatter.F90.current
  ! edit ice_gather_scatter.F90, replace subroutines with GatherScatter_all.subr
  diff ice_gather_scatter.F90.current ice_gather_scatter.F90

  ! There may be some extra blank lines or subroutine separators that need to be cleaned up at the
  ! start or end of the replacement code

4. Test and test again

  ! Run both single and multi processor tests and iterate until done.

